        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-06-11T00:29:53.145Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"379\" data-topic=\"19904\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(As, it’s amusing that CC and GL both happen to have their names abbreviated like so considerably more often than most characters.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I always assumed that was a deliberate reference to the obvious similarities between the two.  GL doesn’t even make much sense to use an an abbreviation, considering there are almost always multiple Green Lanterns hanging around Earth and at least one has never been part of the core.  GL is a job title, not a proper supranym.</p>\n<p>CC, in the hand, is much more singular.</p>",
